/* book Worked example: Q: An STS-1 frame is 810 bytes and repeats 8000 times per second. (a) Find the line rate. (b) Find the SPE rate for the 783-byte envelope. (c) What fraction of the frame is transport overhead? (d) What fraction is overhead of any kind if the path overhead column is also counted?
   1. (a) Bits per frame = 810 × 8 = 6480. Line rate = 6480 × 8000 = 51 840 000 b/s = 51.84 Mb/s.
   2. (b) SPE bits per frame = 783 × 8 = 6264. SPE rate = 6264 × 8000 = 50.112 Mb/s.
   3. (c) Transport overhead = 810 − 783 = 27 bytes (3 columns × 9 rows). Fraction = 27/810 = 0.0333 = 3.33 percent, worth 1.728 Mb/s.
   4. (d) Adding the path overhead column: 27 + 9 = 36 bytes. Fraction = 36/810 = 4.44 percent, and 51.84 × (1 − 0.0444) = 49.536 Mb/s is left before the fixed stuff is removed.
   5. Check: 87 + 3 = 90 columns, and 50.112 + 1.728 = 51.84 Mb/s.
   Answer: Line rate 51.84 Mb/s, SPE rate 50.112 Mb/s, transport overhead 3.33 percent, all overhead 4.44 percent. */
