/* book Worked example 2: Q: An STM-1 frame has 270 columns × 9 rows and repeats every 125 µs. (a) Find the STM-1 rate and show it equals three STS-1s. (b) Find the STM-16 rate. (c) Find the VC-4 and C-4 rates. (d) How many E1s does one STM-1 carry, and what is their total rate?
   1. (a) 270 × 9 = 2430 bytes; 2430 × 8 × 8000 = 155.52 Mb/s. Three STS-1s: 3 × 51.84 = 155.52 Mb/s, the same.
   2. (b) STM-16 = 16 × 155.52 = 2488.32 Mb/s, which is OC-48 (48 × 51.84 = 2488.32 Mb/s).
   3. (c) VC-4 = 261 columns: 261 × 9 × 8 × 8000 = 150.336 Mb/s. C-4 = 260 columns: 260 × 9 × 8 × 8000 = 149.76 Mb/s.
   4. (d) The mapping 3 × 7 × 3 gives 63 E1s. Their rate is 63 × 2.048 = 129.024 Mb/s.
   5. Check: 155.52 ÷ 2.048 = 75.9, but only 63 E1s fit, because each E1 sits in a TU-12 of 36 bytes per frame (2.304 Mb/s) with its own overhead and stuffing, and the section overhead takes 9 of the 270 columns.
   Answer: STM-1 = 155.52 Mb/s = 3 × STS-1; STM-16 = 2488.32 Mb/s; VC-4 = 150.336 Mb/s and C-4 = 149.76 Mb/s; 63 E1s carrying 129.024 Mb/s. */
