/* book exam traps: The 810-byte frame belongs to STS-1. An STM-1 (or STS-3) frame is 2430 bytes, 270 × 9, in the same 125 µs. | Do not divide 155.52 Mb/s by 2.048 Mb/s to count E1s; that gives 75.9. The SDH mapping is 3 × 7 × 3 = 63 E1s per STM-1. | Pointer bytes H1, H2 and H3 sit in row 4 of the transport overhead, not inside the SPE. They mark where the floating envelope starts. | The 783-byte SPE still contains the path overhead; transport overhead alone is 3.33 percent, all overhead 4.44 percent. | UPSR/SNCP sends the signal both ways and selects; BLSR/MS-SPRing shares protection capacity and loops back at the cut. Do not swap the two. */
